# - Related commits: [hash]

# --- DOCUMENTATION UPDATES (REQUIRED for code changes) ---
# Updated documentation:
# - DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md: [what was added]
# - PRELIMINARY_REPORT.md: [what was updated]
# - presentationSlide.md: [if milestone]

# --- TYPE OPTIONS ---
# feat:     New feature
# fix:      Bug fix
# docs:     Documentation only changes
# style:    Formatting, missing semicolons, etc (no code change)
# refactor: Code restructuring (no functional change)
# perf:     Performance improvement
# test:     Adding or updating tests
# build:    Changes to build system or dependencies
# ci:       Changes to CI/CD configuration
# chore:    Other changes (e.g., updating .gitignore)

# --- EXAMPLES ---
# fix: Fix Bug #5 - Add node-based threshold methods to validation list
#
# Orthrus was producing 0 TP despite AUC=0.81 because THRESHOLD_METHODS
# validation list was missing node-based threshold methods. Added
# max_val_node_score, mean_val_node_score, and percentile_val_node_score.
#
# Bug #5: Orthrus 0 TP despite good model quality
# Root Cause: Config validation rejected valid threshold methods
# Impact: 0% → 100% precision recovery (10 TP detected)
# Validation: Job 6562381
#
# Updated documentation:
# - DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md: Added Bug #5 with root cause analysis
# - PRELIMINARY_REPORT.md: Updated Day 12 bug fix section

# feat: Implement Kairos queue-level detection (510 lines)
#
# Implements paper-faithful Kairos detection per IEEE S&P'23 §4.3.
# Uses time-window queuing with IDF-based suspicious node extraction
# and overlapping window correlation for queue formation.
#
# Paper citation: KAIROS §4.3.1 (queue formation algorithm)
# Related: Phase 1 implementation sprint
#
# Updated documentation:
# - DEVELOPMENT_HISTORY.md: Added Phase 1 implementation details
# - PRELIMINARY_REPORT.md: Added Day 11 implementation section

